class:: IkedaMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Ikeda map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/HenonMap

description::

Implements Kensuke Ikeda's optical ring-cavity map. It computes code::t = 0.4 - 6/(1+x*x+y*y)::, then rotates and contracts the old coordinate by code::u:: before adding one to x.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, IkedaMap is trigger driven and holds; unlike Stepper, it evolves a coupled rotational recurrence.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::ikeda-map-phase.png#The default Ikeda orbit after its transient. x is horizontal and y is vertical; the folded bands result from contraction and state-dependent rotation.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: u
Map contraction/control parameter; not clipped.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ IkedaMap.ar(Impulse.ar(300))[0] * 0.05 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(IkedaMap.kr(Impulse.kr(16))[1].linexp(-1, 1, 100, 4000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Ikeda map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-0.5, 1.9], [-2.4, 1],
    { IkedaMap.kr(Impulse.kr(80)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-0.5, 1.9).linexp(-0.5, 1.9, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-2.4, 1).linlin(-2.4, 1, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

